data live_tree_disposition: LiveTreeDisposition = SubstrateInputsOnly

// A TAIL STATEMENT `let` REFUSES; THIS MOVES THE REFUSAL ONTO THE LET AND GIVES IT ITS OWN CAUSE.
//
// THE SUBJECT IS THE NATIVE LANE'S NORMALIZE, as in
// v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position and
// v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.let_match_early_return.
//
// v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold reads a STATEMENT let in exactly one place: body_lower_stmt_spine,
// which binds the let's key to its lowered value and the lowered REST of the spine as its body. A let
// that ENDS a statement spine has no following statement to become that body. Before this change the
// spine's Absent arm handed that let to the VALUE reader, which answers any let through the
// door-holder body_lower_let_expr with body_lowering_reason_let_body_not_reachable_from_node -- a
// reason that blames the compiler for a module that wrote a binding with no body, since no let is ever
// a value (body_lower_let_expr refuses on both arms). THE CHANGE refuses at the let itself, with
// body_lowering_reason_statement_let_in_tail_position: the sibling of the `return` arm beside it (a
// `return` that is not in tail position refuses; a `let` that is in tail position refuses). A braced
// block's ONE statement is likewise read by the statement authority rather than the value reader, and
// src/v2/workflow/compile_door_cause_ownership.dag carries the CauseOwnership row for the new cause.
//
// IT CHANGES WHICH REASON REFUSES, AND WHO OWNS IT. It does not make any of these shapes lower, and
// no row here claims one does. The failure the new cause names is already on the record:
// dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode/accepted_source_emits_uncompilable_target.dag carries the INSTANCE
// "a FUNCTION BODY WITH NO TAIL VALUE -- a body of statement lets whose last statement is a `let`,
// under a declared return that is not Unit", witnessed there by an emitted Rust function that rustc
// then refuses with E0308. That instance is on the rust target and is NOT claimed closed here; the same
// shape on this lane's door is what this file pins.
//
// FIXTURE SOURCES LIVE IN THIS CLAIM, NOT ON DISK. Each row's module is carried inline as the `source`
// of a DagSourceReadWitness, and the `path` argument is an artifact LABEL, not a repository file. This
// branch once also materialized each fixture under src/v2/test/fixture/namespace_xl0/ and added a
// source_layout_namespaces row to make those files compilable: two sources for one fact, one of which
// nothing read (the claim never opens a file). The files and the layout row are removed; this claim is
// the single home, so a fixture cannot drift from what is asserted about it.
//
// ONE ROW THE ARCHIVED BRANCH HAD IS WITHDRAWN, NOT RESTORED. It pinned a braced arm block whose tail
// statement opens with a parenthesized expression, as a door-holder refusal. That expectation asserts
// how the parser resolves a line-leading `(` -- a question this suite cannot answer, since the grammar
// declares no statement terminator and exactly one newline-continuation guard (`-`, v2.extdeps.languages
// dag_grammar_additive_newline_minus_guard) -- and a module the seed ACCEPTS authors exactly that shape:
// the line-leading `(` in path_is_under_production_instance_root,
// dag/gunbc/instruments/compute_run_unit_cold.dag. The row recorded a prediction about the parser as if
// it were a reading. Re-pinning it in the other direction would be the same fabrication mirrored, so the
// question -- can a statement expression begin with `(` -- is left open and unrowed until someone RUNS
// the shape.
data lst_ctl_body_let_source: String = "module v2.test.fixture.namespace_xl0.lst_ctl_body_let\n\nfn lst_probe(i: Int) -> Int {\n  let x = i\n  x\n}\n"

data lst_ctl_arm_expr_source: String = "module v2.test.fixture.namespace_xl0.lst_ctl_arm_expr\n\ntype LstS = LstA { v: Int } | LstB\n\nfn lst_probe(s: LstS, i: Int) -> Int { match s {\n  LstA { v: v } => v\n  LstB => i\n} }\n"

data lst_ctl_arm_block_source: String = "module v2.test.fixture.namespace_xl0.lst_ctl_arm_block\n\ntype LstS = LstA { v: Int } | LstB\n\nfn lst_probe(s: LstS, i: Int) -> Int { match s {\n  LstA { v: v } => { v }\n  LstB => i\n} }\n"

data lst_ctl_if_branch_source: String = "module v2.test.fixture.namespace_xl0.lst_ctl_if_branch\n\nfn lst_probe(c: Bool, i: Int) -> Int { if c {\n    let x = i\n    x\n  } else { i } }\n"

data lst_ctl_fn_value_source: String = "module v2.test.fixture.namespace_xl0.lst_ctl_fn_value\n\nfn lst_probe(i: Int) -> Int {\n  let g = fn(x) {\n    let y = x\n    y\n  }\n  i\n}\n"

data lst_tail_let_source: String = "module v2.test.fixture.namespace_xl0.lst_tail_let\n\nfn lst_probe(i: Int) -> Int {\n  let x = i\n}\n"

